_out : int\n1930 |         Number of feature names out.\n1931 | \n1932 |     input_features : array-like of str or None, default=None\n1933 |         Only used to validate feature names with `estimator.feature_names_in_`.\n1934 | \n1935 |     Returns\n1936 |     -------\n1937 |     feature_names_in : ndarray of str or `None`\n1938 |         Feature names in.\n1939 |     \"\"\"\n1940 |     _check_feature_names_in(estimator, input_features, generate_names=False)\n1941 |     estimator_name = estimator.__class__.__name__.lower()\n1942 |     return np.asarray(\n1943 |         [f\"{estimator_name}{i}\" for i in range(n_features_out)], dtype=object\n1944 |     )\n```\n\nFound function `sklearn/neighbors/_lof.py:LocalOutlierFactor.fit`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n258 | def fit(self, X, y=None):\n259 |         \"\"\"Fit the local outlier factor detector from the training dataset.\n260 | \n261 |         Parameters\n262 |         ----------\n263 |         X : {array-like, sparse matrix} of shape (n_samples, n_features) or \\\n264 |                 (n_samples, n_samples) if metric='precomputed'\n265 |             Training data.\n266 | \n267 |         y : Ignored\n268 |             Not used, present for API consistency by convention.\n269 | \n270 |         Returns\n271 |         -------\n272 |         self : LocalOutlierFactor\n273 |             The fitted local outlier factor detector.\n274 |         \"\"\"\n275 |         self._fit(X)\n276 | \n277 |         if self.contamination != \"auto\":\n278 |             if not (0.0 < self.contamination <= 0.5):\n279 |                 raise ValueError(\n280 |                     \"contamination must be in (0, 0.5], got: %f\" % self.contamination\n281 |                 )\n282 | \n283 |         n_samples = self.n_samples_fit_\n284 |         if self.n_neighbors > n_samples:\n285 |             warnings.warn(\n286 |                 \"n_neighbors (%s) is greater than the \"\n287 |                 \"total number of samples (%s). n_neighbors \"\n288 |                 \"will be set to (n_samples - 1) for estimation.\"\n289 |                 % (self.n_neighbors, n_samples)\n290 |             )\n291 |         self.n_neighbors_ = max(1, min(self.n_neighbors, n_samples - 1))\n292 | \n293 |         self._distances_fit_X_, _neighbors_indices_fit_X_ = self.kneighbors(\n294 |             n_neighbors=self.n_neighbors_\n295 |         )\n296 | \n297 |         self._lrd = self._local_reachability_density(\n298 |             self._distances_fit_X_, _neighbors_indices_fit_X_\n299 |         )\n300 | \n301 |         # Compute lof score over training samples to define offset_:\n302 |         lrd_ratios_array = (\n303 |             self._lrd[_neighbors_indices_fit_X_] / self._lrd[:, np.newaxis]\n304 |         )\n305 | \n306 |         self.negative_outlier_factor_ = -np.mean(lrd_ratios_array, axis=1)\n307 | \n308 |         if self.contamination == \"auto\":\n309 |             # inliers score around -1 (the higher, the less abnormal).\n310 |             self.offset_ = -1.5\n311 |         else:\n312 |             self.offset_ = np.percentile(\n313 |                 self.negative_outlier_factor_, 100.0 * self.contamination\n314 |             )\n315 | \n316 |         return self\n```\n\nFound function `sklearn/cross_decomposition/_pls.py:PLSRegression.fit`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n634 | def fit(self, X, Y):\n635 |         \"\"\"Fit model to data.\n636 | \n637 |         Parameters\n638 |         ----------\n639 |         X : array-like of shape (n_samples, n_features)\n640 |             Training vectors, where `n_samples` is the number of samples and\n641 |             `n_features` is the number of predictors.\n642 | \n643 |         Y : array-like of shape (n_samples,) or (n_samples, n_targets)\n644 |             Target vectors, where `n_samples` is the number of samples and\n645 |             `n_targets` is the number of response variables.\n646 | \n647 |