stimator to validate the input for.\n2846 | \n2847 |     X : {array-like, sparse matrix, dataframe} of shape \\\n2848 |             (n_samples, n_features), default='no validation'\n2849 |         The input samples.\n2850 |         If `'no_validation'`, no validation is performed on `X`. This is\n2851 |         useful for meta-estimator which can delegate input validation to\n2852 |         their underlying estimator(s). In that case `y` must be passed and\n2853 |         the only accepted `check_params` are `multi_output` and\n2854 |         `y_numeric`.\n2855 | \n2856 |     y : array-like of shape (n_samples,), default='no_validation'\n2857 |         The targets.\n2858 | \n2859 |         - If `None`, :func:`~sklearn.utils.check_array` is called on `X`. If\n2860 |           the estimator's `requires_y` tag is True, then an error will be raised.\n2861 |         - If `'no_validation'`, :func:`~sklearn.utils.check_array` is called\n2862 |           on `X` and the estimator's `requires_y` tag is ignored. This is a default\n2863 |           placeholder and is never meant to be explicitly set. In that case `X` must be\n2864 |           passed.\n2865 |         - Otherwise, only `y` with `_check_y` or both `X` and `y` are checked with\n2866 |           either :func:`~sklearn.utils.check_array` or\n2867 |           :func:`~sklearn.utils.check_X_y` depending on `validate_separately`.\n2868 | \n2869 |     reset : bool, default=True\n2870 |         Whether to reset the `n_features_in_` attribute.\n2871 |         If False, the input will be checked for consistency with data\n2872 |         provided when reset was last True.\n2873 | \n2874 |         .. note::\n2875 | \n2876 |            It is recommended to call `reset=True` in `fit` and in the first\n2877 |            call to `partial_fit`. All other methods that validate `X`\n2878 |            should set `reset=False`.\n2879 | \n2880 |     validate_separately : False or tuple of dicts, default=False\n2881 |         Only used if `y` is not `None`.\n2882 |         If `False`, call :func:`~sklearn.utils.check_X_y`. Else, it must be a tuple of\n2883 |         kwargs to be used for calling :func:`~sklearn.utils.check_array` on `X` and `y`\n2884 |         respectively.\n2885 | \n2886 |         `estimator=self` is automatically added to these dicts to generate\n2887 |         more informative error message in case of invalid input data.\n2888 | \n2889 |     skip_check_array : bool, default=False\n2890 |         If `True`, `X` and `y` are unchanged and only `feature_names_in_` and\n2891 |         `n_features_in_` are checked. Otherwise, :func:`~sklearn.utils.check_array`\n2892 |         is called on `X` and `y`.\n2893 | \n2894 |     **check_params : kwargs\n2895 |         Parameters passed to :func:`~sklearn.utils.check_array` or\n2896 |         :func:`~sklearn.utils.check_X_y`. Ignored if validate_separately\n2897 |         is not False.\n2898 | \n2899 |         `estimator=self` is automatically added to these params to generate\n2900 |         more informative error message in case of invalid input data.\n2901 | \n2902 |     Returns\n2903 |     -------\n2904 |     out : {ndarray, sparse matrix} or tuple of these\n2905 |         The validated input. A tuple is returned if both `X` and `y` are\n2906 |         validated.\n2907 |     \"\"\"\n2908 |     _check_feature_names(_estimator, X, reset=reset)\n2909 |     tags = get_tags(_estimator)\n2910 |     if y is None and tags.target_tags.required:\n2911 |         raise ValueError(\n2912 |             f\"This {_estimator.__class__.__name__} estimator \"\n2913 |             \"requires y to be passed, but the target y is None.\"\n2914 |         )\n2915 | \n2916 |     no_val_X = isinstance(X, str) and X == \"no_validation\"\n2917 |     no_val_y = y is None or isinstance(y, str) and y == \"no_validation\"\n2918 | \n2919 |     if no_val_X and no_val_y:\n2920 |         raise ValueError(\"Validation should be done on X, y or both.\")\n2921 | \n2922 |     default_check_params = {\"estimator\": _estimator}\n2923 |     check_params = {**default_check_params, **check_params}\n2924 | \n2925 |     if skip_check_array:\n2926 |         if not no_val_X and no_val_y:\n2927 |             out = X\n2928 |         elif no_val_X and not no_val_y:\n2929 |             out = y\n2930 |         else:\n2931 |             out = X, y\n2932 |     elif not no_val_X and no_val_y:\n2933 |         out = check_array(X, input_name=\"X\", **check_params)\n2934 |     elif no_val_X and not no_val_y:\n2935 |         out = _check_y(y, **check_params)\n2936 |     else:\n2937 |         if validate_separately:\n2938 |             # We need this because some estimators validate X and y\n2939 |             # separately, and in general, separately calling check_array()\n2940 |             # on X and y isn't equivalent to just calling check_X_y()\n2941 |             # :(\n2942 |             check_X_params, check_y_params = validate_separately\n2943 |             if \"estimator\" not in check_X_params:\n2944 |                 check_X_params = {**default_check_params, **check_X_params}\n2945 |             X = check_array(X, input_name=\"X\", **check_X_params)\n2946 |             if \"estimator\" not in check_y_params:\n2947 |                 check_y_params = {**default_check_params, **check_y_params}\n2948 |             y = check_array(y, input_name=\"y\", **check_y_params)\n2949 |         else:\n2950 |             X, y = check_X_y(X, y, **check_params)\n2951 |         out = X, y\n2952 | \n2953 |     if not no_val_X and check_params.get(\"ensure_2d\", True):\n2954 |         _check_n_features(_estimator, X, reset=reset)\n2955 | \n2956 |     return out\n```\n\nFound function `sklearn/multiclass.py:OneVsRestClassifier.__sklearn_tags__`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n600 | def __sklearn_tags__(self):\n601 |         \"\"\"Indicate if wrapped estimator is using a precomputed Gram matrix\"\"\"\n602 |         tags = super().__sklearn_tags_