s styling fails.\n596 | \n597 |     This can be due to the styling not having an equivalent value or because the\n598 |     styling isn't properly formatted.\n599 | \n600 |     See Also\n601 |     --------\n602 |     DataFrame.style : Returns a Styler object for applying CSS-like styles.\n603 |     io.formats.style.Styler : Helps style a DataFrame or Series according to the\n604 |         data with HTML and CSS.\n605 |     io.formats.style.Styler.to_excel : Export styled DataFrame to Excel.\n606 |     io.formats.style.Styler.to_html : Export styled DataFrame to HTML.\n607 | \n608 |     Examples\n609 |     --------\n610 |     >>> df = pd.DataFrame({\"A\": [1, 1, 1]})\n611 |     >>> df.style.map(lambda x: \"background-color: blueGreenRed;\").to_excel(\n612 |     ...     \"styled.xlsx\"\n613 |     ... )  # doctest: +SKIP\n614 |     CSSWarning: Unhandled color format: 'blueGreenRed'\n615 |     >>> df.style.map(lambda x: \"border: 1px solid red red;\").to_excel(\n616 |     ...     \"styled.xlsx\"\n617 |     ... )  # doctest: +SKIP\n618 |     CSSWarning: Unhandled color format: 'blueGreenRed'\n619 |     \"\"\"\n```\n"}, {"content": "Let me explore the tree structure to understand the dependencies and implementation flow:\n\n<function=explore_tree_structure>\n<parameter=start_entities>['pandas/core/generic.py:NDFrame.to_excel']</parameter>\n<parameter=direction>both</parameter>\n<parameter=dependency_type_filter>['imports', 'invokes']</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "explore_tree_structure", "content": "OBSERVATION:\npandas/core/generic.py:NDFrame.to_excel\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 imports \u2500\u2500 pandas/io/formats/excel.py:ExcelFormatter\n\u2502              \u251c\u2500\u2500 invokes \u2500\u2500 pandas/io/formats/excel.py:CSSToExcelConverter\n\u2502              \u251c\u2500\u2500 invokes \u2500\u2500 pandas/core/indexes/base.py:Index\n\u2502              \u251c\u2500\u2